From: vaughanb <brenden.vaughan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] CharacterDataCache: drop the finalizer that released
 pooled collections off the main thread

~CharacterDataCache called CleanCacheData, which returns the cache's pooled
dictionaries to UnityEngine.Pool's CollectionPool. Finalizers run on the
garbage collector's finalizer thread, and those pools are static and not
synchronised, so a release there can interleave with Get and Release on the
main thread: Get can hand out null, and one collection can be handed out
twice. Under load this shows up as a NullReferenceException inside the pool's
release, "Collecton is null" errors while combining damages, and "Collection
was modified" when two damage results turn out to be the same dictionary.

A cache dropped without CleanCacheData now leaves its collections to the
garbage collector instead of the pool; the pool only loses their reuse. The
rest of the finalizer cleared lists the cache allocated itself, which the
collector frees anyway. CleanCacheData is unchanged and still runs on the
main thread when a character is re-cached.
---
 Core/Scripts/MemoryManagement/Caching/CharacterDataCache.cs | 13 -------------
 1 file changed, 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Core/Scripts/MemoryManagement/Caching/CharacterDataCache.cs b/Core/Scripts/MemoryManagement/Caching/CharacterDataCache.cs
index 48de187..f27d77e 100644
--- a/Core/Scripts/MemoryManagement/Caching/CharacterDataCache.cs
+++ b/Core/Scripts/MemoryManagement/Caching/CharacterDataCache.cs
@@ -108,19 +108,6 @@ namespace MultiplayerARPG
             LeftHandWeaponAbilityIndexes = new Dictionary<string, int>();
         }
 
-        ~CharacterDataCache()
-        {
-            CleanCacheData();
-            RightHandWeaponAbilities.Clear();
-            RightHandWeaponAbilities = null;
-            RightHandWeaponAbilityIndexes.Clear();
-            RightHandWeaponAbilityIndexes = null;
-            LeftHandWeaponAbilities.Clear();
-            LeftHandWeaponAbilities = null;
-            LeftHandWeaponAbilityIndexes.Clear();
-            LeftHandWeaponAbilityIndexes = null;
-        }
-
         private void CleanCacheData()
         {
             // Release buffs
